## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of attention scaling, memory constraints, and practical trade-offs in production-grade transformers.

## Key Concepts
- Block-local attention and memory scaling
- Attention masking within a window
- Q/K/V reshaping for block processing
- Trade-offs: accuracy vs latency vs memory

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: local attention in blocks
function localAttention(Q, K, V, block=256, window=128){
  // Q,K,V: [B, T, D]
  const B = Q.length, T = Q[0].length, D = Q[0][0].length;
  let O = Array.from({length:B}, () => Array.from({length:T}, () => new Array(D).fill(0)));
  for (let b=0; b<B; b++){
    for (let s=0; s<T; s+=block){
      const end = Math.min(T, s+block);
      for (let t=s; t<end; t++){
        const wStart = Math.max(0, t-window);
        const wEnd = Math.min(T, t+window+1);
        // compute attention over [wStart, wEnd)
        // A = softmax((Q[t]·K[w].T)/sqrt(D))
        // O[b][t] = sum_{w=wStart}^{wEnd-1} A[w]·V[w]
      }
    }
  }
  return O;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How does changing window size affect long-range dependency capture and memory?
- What metrics would you monitor to detect degradation when switching from global to local attention?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to translate a real-world costing task into a reproducible, beginner-friendly LangChain planning flow that uses tool orchestration and simple arithmetic.

## Key Concepts

- Tool selection and orchestration
- Planning vs. execution, simple ReAct-like flow
- Cost estimation: hourly to monthly, data transfer edges, taxes
- Fallbacks for missing pricing data

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal planning snippet illustrating tool invocation
async function planCost(query){
  const prices = await pricingApi.getPrices({services:["EC2","RDS","CloudFront"], instance:"t4g.medium"});
  const monthly = prices.ec2 * 730 + prices.rds * 730 + prices.cloudfront * 730;
  return monthly;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle data-transfer costs and regional multipliers?
- What changes if pricing data is incomplete or delayed?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical understanding of attention math, dimensions, scaling, and how tokenization affects token-to-token alignment in real models.

## Key Concepts

- Dot-product attention math and scaling (√d_k)
- Softmax over keys for each query
- Tokenization impact on alignment
- Practical pitfalls in batching

## Code Example

```javascript
function simpleAttention(q, k, v) {
  // q: [d], k: [n, d], v: [n, d]
  const scores = k.map(row => dot(q, row) / Math.sqrt(d));
  const weights = softmax(scores);
  return weights.reduce((acc, w, idx) => acc + w * v[idx], 0);
}
```

