## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical understanding of retrieval-augmented NLP basics using a concrete tech stack (MongoDB Atlas Vector Search) and a beginner-friendly workflow.

## Key Concepts
- Chunking strategy for long docs
- Embedding models and cosine similarity
- Vector database indexing and search
- Simple result assembly and error handling

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example chunking
function chunkText(text, maxChars=512){
  const words = text.split(/\\s+/);
  let chunk = '', chunks = [];
  for (const w of words){
    if ((chunk + ' ' + w).length > maxChars){
      chunks.push(chunk.trim()); chunk = w;
    } else {
      chunk += ' ' + w;
    }
  }
  if (chunk) chunks.push(chunk.trim());
  return chunks;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle overlapping chunks to preserve context?
- How would you validate results when the top-k chunks disagree?
